comment.narrative:
The target value for this indicator has been reached.
This indicator is collected through the activities listed below.
Under the PPI, 10,958 producers benefited from common services, including 1,312 women, distributed as follows:
1.	9,083 producers trained, including 1,058 through farmer field schools (FFS);
2.	1,875 farmers, including 254 women beneficiaries for agricultural services on 2,178.1 hectares;
Support was provided on: 
1.	Capacity building for learners;
2.	manual harvesting of bunches using scissors; 
3.	manual harvesting of bunches with sickles;
4.	mechanized pruning;
5.	phytosanitary diagnosis.

Under the PPI, 603 farmers received support during cluster and technician training, including 50 women. They are distributed as follows: 
533 farmers, including 40 women from the first cohort;
75 farmers, including 10 women from the second cohort;

