This indicator will be informed on the basis of comparative studies based on the data of the baseline evaluation with those of an evaluation carried out on a sample that has benefited from the actions listed below:
1.	support for the improvement of fruit production and quality through better control of fruit fly pressure and training of stakeholders;
2.	the development of shea butter (via Marque Collective) and Kent mango (via Protected Geographical Indication) through intellectual property;
3.	exports of finished products (mango puree, juice and concentrate and shea butter meeting international standards) resulting from the establishment of industrial mango and oilseed processing units; 
4.	Support from the CÃ´te d'Ivoire Export Agency (ACIEX) for the export of 25 SMEs
As all the activities listed above are currently in the start-up phase, the collection of basic data is planned for the second half of 2025.
